# secrets — never commit keys
*.pem
*.key
*.p12

# local env
.env

# Pi project-local package installs + marketplace cache (generated on startup from .pi/settings.json)
.pi/npm/
.pi/git/

# pi MCP override — pi reads the project .mcp.json through pi-mcp-adapter; a local .pi/mcp.json is never committed
.pi/mcp.json

# Claude Code runtime lock (session-local, never committed)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# plans — working docs, never committed; directory kept via .gitkeep
plan/*
!plan/.gitkeep

# Local-state classes — per-machine / per-run ephemera that live IN the project
# tree but must never be version-controlled. Modelled on charly/.gitignore (the
# same class list; charly's parity gate checks only the 5 byte-identical shared
# files, not this file), adapted to what the umbrella root actually produces:
#   .check/        — `charly check run check-all-beds` (the root roster) writes its
#                    run artifacts + NOTES.md here; without this the root tree reads
#                    dirty after every roster run (and risks an accidental commit of
#                    per-run state). NOTE: `charly task verify` does NOT check the
#                    root tree — it asserts each SUBMODULE's cleanliness — so this is
#                    about an honest root `git status`, not a gate.
#   .build/        — generated Containerfiles from `charly box generate`.
#   .opencharly/   — deploy-state output from `charly deploy add`.
#   image/         — built VM disk/seed artifacts (`charly vm build`; the
#                    configurable vm.image_dir root, default `image`).
#   .containerignore / .dockerignore — generated build-context ignore files
#                    (`charly box generate` from defaults.context_ignore).
#   scratchpad/    — per-session temporary files.
#   .worktrees/    — per-session linked feature worktrees under the umbrella
#                    (<umbrella>/.worktrees/<slug>/<repo>/), the harness-neutral
#                    session model (AGENTS.md "The development model"); the tracked
#                    submodule checkouts stay clean at their gitlinks.
#   bin/           — a worktree-local built binary.
.check/
.build/
.opencharly/
image/
.containerignore
.dockerignore
scratchpad/
.worktrees/
bin/
*.sync-conflict-*

# Python bytecode. The reasonix code extension (`.reasonix/plugin/sidecar.py`) is
# Python, so running its own handshake test — the check documented in
# `.reasonix/plugin/README.md` — leaves a `__pycache__/` directory behind. Left
# untracked-but-unignored it shows up as dirt in `git status` and `verify`, a
# self-inflicted failure with no tracked file to explain it.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
